-- title:
--   Integrality over the plane local ring at (a,a^q)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $q$, a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, a field $k$ of characteristic $q$ with decidable equality, a ring homomorphism $\mathrm{red} : A \to k$, and an element $a \in k$. Let $f$ belong to `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)`, the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}((X))$ obtained by adjoining to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ the coefficientwise images of the full modular function field of level $1\cdot q$. Assume: (h₁) the Laurent series $f$ lies in `CharPReduction.modularLocalized (1 * q) A.toSubring red`, the localisation of the subring generated by the constant series from $A$ together with the two $j$-series at level $1\cdot q$, inverting those of its elements whose reduction under $\mathrm{red}$ is nonzero; (h₂) the same holds for the image of $f$ under `frickeInvolutionBar (1 * q)`, the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the Fricke involution of the full level-$1\cdot q$ function field; (hpole) for every place $W$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar (1 * q)` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ (a proper valuation subring, containing the image of the base field, whose ideals are principal) at which $\mathrm{ord}_W f < 0$, it is not the case that both there is $x \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,x = a$ and $\mathrm{ord}_W(j - x) > 0$, and there is $y \in A$ with $\mathrm{red}\,y = a^q$ and $\mathrm{ord}_W(j_q - y) > 0$; here $j$ is the $q$-expansion `jq` transported coefficientwise to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $j_q$ its image under `qExpand ℚ (1 * q)`, and $\mathrm{ord}_W$ is the negative of the logarithm of the associated discrete valuation. The conclusion is that the Laurent series $f$ is integral over `NodeLocalized.modularLocalizedAtPoint (1 * q) A.toSubring red a (a ^ q)`: the subring of those Laurent series $g$ for which $g \cdot \mathrm{modularEval}(s) = \mathrm{modularEval}(r)$ for some $r, s$ in the polynomial ring in two variables over $A$ with the value of $s$ at $(a, a^q)$ after reduction nonzero.
--
--   This is the normality half of the analysis of $X_0(q)$ at a node of its special fibre: a function whose divisor of poles misses both the special fibre (expressed by membership in the two Gauss-type rings, for $f$ and for its Fricke image) and every place whose $(j, j_q)$-coordinates reduce to $(a, a^q)$ is regular at the points above that closed point, hence integral over the local ring of the plane model given by the modular equation. It is used in the lemmas producing values of functions at the Frobenius node pair, namely [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_and_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_pole_not_centred`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_and_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_pole_not_centred), [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_pole_not_centred`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_forall_pole_not_centred) and [`ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_mem_ssJSet_of_pow_eq`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_hasValue_frobNodePair_of_mem_ssJSet_of_pow_eq).
